            <div xml:id="d531">

                <pb facs="0860" n="724" xml:id="pg724"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/3251: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Moore</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-01-04T15:00:00-05:00">January 4, 1929—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:55 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>2. Your 1, January 3, 8 p.m. On January 9, Ralph Cady and assistant, Julio del
                    Pino, will sail from Callao for Arica. Señor del Pino is a Peruvian citizen.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Moore</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
